  "notes": "Built 1770 by Cornelis Rauws in Louis XVI / classicist style after the 1663 gate collapsed in 1769; only surviving 18th-century Amsterdam gate (Sint Antoniespoort/Waag is 15th century). Flat-roofed rectangular building, raised centre with balustrade crowned by an octagonal dome tower; sandstone gate passages framed as a triumphal arch and covered by pediments. City side has recessed Doric pilasters on rustica and the old Amsterdam arms (ship); land side has banded columns and the new arms (three St Andrew's crosses). Free-standing on the Alexanderplein since 1903, so no adjacent neighbours are suppressed. Suppress only the exact parent aliases (w45038672 / BAG pand); bridges, canals and the square remain."
